    "sentence_translations": [
      "Small People",
      "",
      "One day, Little Le said to Paul: “Paul, you're so tall!”",
      "Paul said: “It's not that I'm tall, it's because you are all small people.”",
      "When Little Le heard this, she got angry and walked away.",
      "",
      "Paul was confused: I just wanted to say that Chinese girls are relatively short and cute.",
      "How come Little Le got so angry?",
      "",
      "That is because in Chinese, “small person” also has another meaning.",
      "It refers to someone who “likes to tell on people”, and is not a good word.",
      "Even though “small person” formerly also meant a “small grown person” or “child”, nowadays it is rarely used.",
      "Nowadays, when Chinese people hear the word “small person”, they will assume they're being scolded.",
      "So when Little Le heard Paul calling her a “small person”, of course she got angry.",
      ""
